3e79237bd","position":"1786900640105112001-409756f3-303d-49c8-89e1-1d99fa02b800"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review BLOCK identified an actual artifact-location conflict: the current skill names `.rebar-janitor/`, while this repo’s surviving reports/tools/known-fine ledger live in `.joe-janitor/`. Recovery will use `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`, matching recorded file impact, and will carry a prominent RECOVERED / NOT A NATIVE RUN banner. The plan will also identify the protocol version visible in the transcript/history and split compound acceptance criteria before re-review.","timestamp":1786897562314341001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Recovery complete. Artifact: `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` (671 lines), headed `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN`; it remains local-only under the repository’s established `.joe-janitor/` convention. Recovered run totals: 82 Discovery candidates; 54 Verification survivors (45 DEFECT, 9 HARDENING); 28 drops; 28 Remediation moves (21 agent-converged, 6 research-resolved, 1 no-consensus). The export preserves only RP-01 through RP-06. All six were approved: RP-02 as proposed; RP-01/RP-03/RP-04/RP-05/RP-06 with material refinements. The report includes transcript/repository/tracker/external evidence labels, exact source-tree corroboration at b0aac231, prior-decision context, approval status, rationale, recovery confidence, and explicit unrecoverable fields. RP-07–RP-28 were never presented before the transcript ended. Phase 5 was never reached; no cleanup epic/children or known-fine changes exist, and none were invented during recovery. No production code changed; `git diff --name-only` is empty.","timestamp":1786900480933448001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Local-only recovery artifact verification (2026-08-16 America/Los_Angeles):\n\nArtifact: `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`\nSHA-256: `c8a382504f15c591505df56fd55d3c5a84313f3eb57c9c4dd71153c350426cd6`\n\nConcrete checks from `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar`:\n- `rtk wc -l .joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` -> `671`\n- `rtk sed -n '1,5p' ...` -> first line `# RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN`\\n- heading count query over `^### Decision [1-6] / RP-0[1-6]$|^## Phase [1-5] ` -> `11` (six decision records + five phase sections)\\n- `rtk git diff --name-only` -> empty; no production-code changes\\n\\nThe six decision records each contain an evidence record, recovered rationale, final Phase-4 verdict, approved refinement, explicit recovery confidence/uncertainty, and source-labeled transcript/repository/tracker/external evidence. The five phase sections name missing/unrecoverable outputs and historical/inferred mappings. Phase 5 records that exact-title tracker searches found no cleanup epic/children and that none were created during recovery. The report is intentionally git-excluded under the established `.joe-janitor/` convention, so this ticket comment is the durable attestation channel for those criteria.","timestamp":1786900640105112001}],"created_at":1786897281080091001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nThe generated artifacts from a rebar-janitor session were lost. Reconstruct the recoverable results from `~/Downloads/ChatGPT-Rebar janitor analysis-20260816-0915.md`. Decisions 1-6 require the deepest research and analysis. This is a no-code recovery: preserve evidence, distinguish transcript facts from present-day corroboration, and make uncertainty explicit.\n\nThe current skill names `.rebar-janitor/`, but this repository’s historical local-only artifact convention is `.joe-janitor/`, evidenced by tracked `.joe-janitor/tools.md` and tracker record `naive-bigheaded-wildcat`. Other git-excluded files visible in one checkout are opportunistic corroboration only: the plan does not assume that `known-fine.md` or prior `report-*.md` files survive. The deterministic output is the intentionally git-excluded local artifact `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md`. Its title and opening banner must say `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` so future runs cannot mistake reconstructed material for an original Phase-2 record. Report-content criteria are operator-attested because repository-snapshot verifiers intentionally cannot see local-only janitor reports; checksum and structural evidence are recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory the source transcript, its structure, and any surviving repository/tracker evidence without modifying production code.\n- Identify the rebar-janitor protocol version in effect during the transcript from its content and repository history; use the current protocol as a guide, labeling inferred mappings if the historical structure differs.\n- Reconstruct the Phase 1/2 finding and verification context needed to interpret the later decisions.\n- Recover decisions 1-6 individually, tracing evidence, prior decisions, competing remediation proposals, convergence/divergence, approval state, and ticketization status where available.\n- Cross-check material claims against the repository, ADRs, commit history, and ticket store. Perform external research when a recovered decision relies on a community-practice claim that the transcript or repository cannot substantiate; otherwise label the claim transcript-only.\n- Recover later decisions and phase summaries to the extent supported, clearly labeling gaps and confidence.\n- Write `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` with the recovery banner and record its checksum, structure, and conclusions on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 has a recovered evidence record.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 states its recovered rationale.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 states its approval status.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Each of decisions 1-6 carries an explicit confidence or uncertainty label.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Claims in the report label their source as transcript, repository, tracker, or external research.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The report maps the current protocol’s five phases and labels any historical divergence or inferred mapping.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The report explicitly names missing phase outputs.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Existing decision-to-ticket mappings are listed without creating duplicate remediation tickets.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md` exists with the `RECOVERED — NOT A NATIVE JANITOR RUN` banner.\n- [ ] No production-code file is modified.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A ticket comment records the recovery conclusions and exact artifact path.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".joe-janitor/report-2026-08-16-recovered.md","reason":"Recovered audit/remediation/approval record reconstructed from the surviving transcript"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"56d56214-0d44-46df-8131-c910bdd72b84","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","recovery","audit"],"ticket_id":"ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75","ticket_type":"task","title":"Recover lost rebar-janitor results from 2026-08-16 transcript","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4d6d36f9-c966-4c66-bdda-de6de35cf855","9f3b7a2d-66f9-4017-b0fd-41711ec98e1e","97fdad0f-dc02-41cc-9740-b12543acfbf3","c70f2663-6883-48eb-b73e-2997402448b8","e212dc76-cc10-4c03-a84a-de423b266c8f","27555863-894f-4841-9c65-f176c1dd3623","56d56214-0d44-46df-8131-c910bdd72b84","04e8c416-21c5-4524-b078-37d615e3244e","282c1234-883b-4c40-8e42-39bfe6935fc1","814ea89a-3611-4d94-86d3-a4314b41d380","409756f3-303d-49c8-89e1-1d99fa02b800"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786900640105112002,"uuid":"3cedb0f1-2d3f-46f7-a162-d7103ec8f783"}